i</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Pecoraro</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Cantarini</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonapace</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Np95 is implicated in pericentromeric heterochromatin replication and in major satellite silencing</article-title><source>Mol Biol Cell</source><year>2007</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>1098</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17182844</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1091/mbc.E06-09-0874</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quivy</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Roche</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirschner</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Tagami</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakatani</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Almouzni</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A CAF-1 dependent pool of HP1 during heterochromatin duplication</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>2004</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>3516</fpage><lpage>26</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15306854</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.emboj.7600362</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sengupta</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Camps</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mathews</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Barenboim-Stapleton</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Nguyen</surname><given-names>QT</given-names></name><name><surname>Difilippantonio</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ried</surname><given-names>T</given-name